---
layout: artIndex
title: Art
override:tags: []
---

<div class="gallery">
  <div>
    <p>For art, you can tag things individually, and/or you can make a json file in a folder to automatically tag everything in that folder with one or more tags! You can mix and match the methods, however you want. This then automatically makes tagged pages, with a matching alphabeticized tag list on the side.</p>
    <p>The consectetur, dolor, and ipsum folders have an example of a folder-wide tag. lorem and sit-amet have examples of manual tags. /consectetur/500-700/ has an example of mix and match.</p>
  </div>
  
  {% for art in collections.artwork reversed %}
    <div class="gallery-card">
      <a href="{{ art.url }}">
        <figure>
          <img loading="lazy" src="{{ art.data.src }}">
          <figcaption>{{ art.data.title }}</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </a>
    </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>